Z||000000||rogergarrison||12-06-2001||12:28 PM||||Just wondered if anyone ever tried just connecting the radio cable to the rear window defrost strips? I should think it work work pretty well, and make use of an otherwise usless option. You would have to make sure you disconnected it from power from the defrost switch. The coax would only require the outter braid be grounded to car and the center wire connected to the wire tab.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000001||JohnF||12-06-2001||12:33 PM||||Hmmmmmm!   Let us know how that turns out!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-06-2001||12:37 PM||||Sounds like it could work, many newer cars come with the antenna in the windsheild, in the tinted sunvisor part.  It's just a big bar impregnated in the glass that stretches almost all the way across.  If I had a rear window defogger, I would probably try it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||12-06-2001||12:52 PM||||The rear window defogger uses resistance wire...I really don't know if that's a problem, but it would seem like it would adversely affect the performance.<P>If it were me, I would try using the press-in rain gutters as antennas...they are metal, aren't they ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||12-06-2001||02:06 PM||||If your car has a sunroof, there is a metal molding that goes around the opening. I think it's the one that the rubber trim and headliner fabric gets pressed into. I saw a web site, a while back, describing using this molding as an antenna. Supposed to work well. <BR>I'll post a link if I can find it again.<P>The defroster grid will probably work too, since there isn't any real voltage or current draw involved. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||12-06-2001||02:36 PM||||i just mounted my flexable antenna in the wiper assembly box. (fiberglassed where the antenna used to be) the rear defrost isn't a bad idea. it worked in the 60-70s... why not now.. why did they stop doing that anyway?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||12-06-2001||06:28 PM||||I'll try to find some more information and let you know.  I was planning on running a wire under the fender, but I'd do it this way if it'd work.  I planned on using the switch space for a nitrous arming switch anyway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'll try to find out some more about it. ||||reg||1
